00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:10.400
But there is one that I think is a good to start with.
但有一个片段我觉得很适合作为开场。

316
00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.200
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

317
00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:12.640
Can we hear it, Sam?
我们能听听看吗，Sam？

318
00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.440
Cheryl and Elizabeth from Connecticut.
来自康涅狄格州的 Cheryl 和 Elizabeth。

319
00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:17.240
Hi.
嗨。

320
00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:17.700
Yep.
对。

321
00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.520
And what does the office mean to you?
《办公室》对你们来说意味着什么？

322
00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:20.460
Levity.
轻松幽默。

323
00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.980
And she brings levity to the office every day now.
现在她每天都给办公室带来轻松幽默。

324
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.800
Yeah, I literally am not allowed to say that's what she said anymore.
对啊，我简直不能再讲“她刚才就是这么说的”这个梗了。

325
00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:26.920
Yeah.
对。

326
00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.560
Wait, do you two work together?
等等，你们俩一起工作吗？

327
00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:30.660
In reverse friends.
倒过来的朋友。

328
00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.320
In reverse friends.
倒过来的朋友。

329
00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:31.880
Oh my God.
天哪。

330
00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:33.700
That's so cool.
太酷了吧。

331
00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.140
It's like the office and office ladies combined.
就像 Office 和 Office Ladies 的结合体。

332
00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:38.360
Aw.
噢。

333
00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:39.660
Cheryl and Elizabeth.
Cheryl 和 Elizabeth。

334
00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.220
They're BFFs that work together.
她们是同事兼最佳闺蜜。

335
00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:43.160
That's so sweet.
太贴心了。

336
00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.920
I like that they have rules though.
不过我挺喜欢她们还有规矩的。

337
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.180
You can't say that's what she said.
不能说“她刚才就是这么说的”。

338
00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:54.520
The other clip I wanted to start off with is this clip from Julia, who is a huge office ladies fan.
我想开场用的另一个片段是 Julia 的这段，她是一个超级 Office Ladies 粉丝。

339
00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:55.280
Great.
太好了。

340
00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:56.540
My name's Julia.
我叫 Julia。

341
00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:57.880
And what are you wearing?
你穿着什么呢？

342
00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.180
So I've got my teapot earrings.
我戴着茶壶耳环。

343
00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.540
I've got the PAMs.
我穿着 PAMs T恤。

344
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.560
And then, of course, my podcast merch here, my scarf.
然后，当然还有我的播客周边，这条围巾。

345
00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:08.900
Do you have a favorite office ladies episode or moment?
你有什么最喜欢的 Office Ladies 单集或者时刻吗？

346
00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:18.960
I love the Booze Cruise episode where Greg Daniels talks about, you know, what are people saying they're doing versus what they're doing and how to catch that.
我超爱《游船派对》那一集，Greg Daniels 谈到，你知道的，人们嘴上说在做什么和他们实际在做什么，以及如何识破这一点。

347
00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.980
You learn so much on the podcaSt.
你在播客里能学到好多东西。

348
00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.700
What does the office mean to you?
《办公室》对你意味着什么？

349
00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:30.200
The office is home and I feel most like myself when I'm listening to the podcast on my Wednesday walk.
《办公室》就是家，当我在周三散步时听着播客，我感觉最像真正的自己。

350
00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:30.800
Yay!
耶！

351
00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.440
Every time I hear when someone shares that they listen to the, you know,
每当我听到有人分享说他们在散步或通勤时听这个，你知道的，

352
00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:43.780
podcast on their walk or in their commute and just know that we fill that time for them and we're a happy place for them, I love it so much.
播客，并且知道我们为他们填补了那段时间，我们是他们快乐的源泉，我都爱极了。

353
00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:48.580
I think it's so sweet that she was wearing so much of our merch, Angela, because you work so hard on it.
我觉得她穿了那么多我们的周边真的很贴心，安吉拉，因为你为之付出了那么多心血。

354
00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.200
I do love merch.
我是真的很喜欢周边。

355
00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:54.720
And when I see anyone in an office lady sweatshirt or anything, I do geek out.
而且每当我看到有人穿着办公室女士的卫衣或者别的什么，我真的会兴奋不已。

356
00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:56.000
I always comment on it.
我总是会去搭话。

357
00:13:56.000 --> 00:14:00.000
Well, at the stage door, people would wear our merch and like the tattoos.
对啊，在舞台门外，人们会穿着我们的周边，还有纹身什么的。

358
00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.280
If anybody was wearing our merch, I asked if I could take a picture and send it to you.
如果有人穿着我们的周边，我都会问能不能拍张照发给你。

359
00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:08.400
One woman wore our office lady's apron.
有个女人还穿着我们的办公室女士围裙。

360
00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:10.320
Our apron lady.
我们的围裙女士。

361
00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.020
That's traveling back in time.
那简直是时光倒流。

362
00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:12.700
I know.
就是说啊。

363
00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:17.860
I believe her name was Vera and she also gave me some gooey butter cake from St. Louis.
我记得她好像叫维拉，她还送了我一些来自圣路易斯的黏稠黄油蛋糕。

364
00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:18.940
So thank you, Vera.
所以谢谢你，维拉。

365
00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.440
Well, why don't we take a break?
那么，我们为什么不休息一下呢？

366
00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:24.320
And when we come back, we're going to share some more stories from the convention and the stage door.
等我们回来后，我们将分享更多来自大会和舞台门的幕后故事。

367
00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:32.700
Some really amazing fan encounters, including Cassie and I have a story for you about a couple that got married at the convention.
一些非常棒的粉丝奇遇，包括卡西和我有个故事要讲给你们听，关于一对在大会上结婚的情侣。

368
00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:33.620
At the convention?
在大会上？

369
00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:34.120
Yes.
对。

370
00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:37.400
And there might have been an office cast member that officiated.
而且可能还有一位《办公室》的演员来担任证婚人。

371
00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:38.480
Oh, my goodness.
哦，天哪。

372
00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:39.640
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

373
00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:49.820
All right.
好啦。

374
00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:50.480
We are back.
我们回来了。

375
00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.080
And, Jenna, Cassie and I have quite a story for you all.
珍娜，卡西和我有一个很棒的故事要讲给大家听。

376
00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:58.020
It was the first time ever at the office convention that two people got married.
这是《办公室》大会历史上头一次有两个人结婚。

377
00:14:58.320 --> 00:14:58.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

378
00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.660
Andy Buckley was the officiate.
安迪·巴克利担任了证婚人。

379
00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.940
David Wallace.
大卫·华莱士。

380
00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:03.680
Uh-huh.
呃哼。

381
00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.440
Amazing.
太神奇了。

382
00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:11.680
So Ryan, a Dwight cosplayer, got married to his fiancée, Cora, who is also a cosplayer.
所以瑞安，一个扮演德怀特的coser，和他的未婚妻科拉结婚了，科拉也是个coser。

383
00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:16.180
And for the wedding, the two of them dressed up as Angela Martin and Dwight Schrute.
为了这场婚礼，他俩分别打扮成了安吉拉·马丁和德怀特·舒鲁特。

384
00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:16.880
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

385
00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:17.680
Amazing.
太棒了。

386
00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:23.020
And for any of you guys listening who haven't been to conventions, cosplaying is very popular.
对于任何还没去过大会的听众来说，cosplay非常流行。

387
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.120
People dress up as their favorite characters.
人们会打扮成他们最喜欢的角色。

388
00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:26.180
They go all out.
他们会全力以赴。

389
00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:26.980
Yeah.
对。

390
00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:27.860
Yeah.
对。

391
00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.560
Ryan even reserved a booth.
瑞安甚至预定了一个展位。

392
00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:31.640
And he set up a Dwight desk.
他还搭建了一个德怀特的工作台。

393
00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:39.160
And it had Dwight's little placard and computer phone, a jello mold with a stapler in it.
上面有德怀特的小铭牌、座机电话，还有一个里面装着订书机的果冻模具。

394
00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.360
And it was so cool.
这太酷了。

395
00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:42.700
People could take pictures with him at the desk.
人们可以坐在桌子旁跟他合影。

396
00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.300
And I loved talking with him.
我特别喜欢跟他聊天。

397
00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:50.080
And here's a clip of him explaining how he ended up getting married at the convention on Sunday morning.
下面是一段他的录音剪辑，讲述他是如何在周日上午最终在大会上结婚的。

398
00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:53.120
So, I had plans to get married this year.
所以，我原本计划今年结婚。

399
00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:56.140
I actually proposed in front of Weird Al last year.
我实际上是在去年“怪人阿尔”的面前求婚的。

400
00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:58.100
I made him part of the proposal.
我让他参与到了求婚过程中。

401
00:15:58.360 --> 00:15:59.280
He kind of helped me out.
他帮了我个忙。

402
00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:02.900
About a month and a half ago, I reached out to Andy Buckley.
大约一个半月前，我联系了安迪·巴克利。

403
00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.540
Not expecting anything.
没抱什么期望。

404
00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:08.240
I just said, hey, would you be interested?
我只是说，嘿，你会有兴趣吗？

405
00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.380
Like, it's the last reunion.
比如，这是最后一次聚会了。

406
00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.580
And I really want to do something special.
我真的很想做点特别的事情。

407
00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.080
I'm planning on getting married anyway.
我本来就打算结婚。

408
00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.720
It'll be the two-year anniversary of when we met.
那将是我们相识两周年的纪念日。

409
00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:20.760
Do you think you would be interested in marrying us at the reunion?
你觉得你有兴趣在聚会上给我们主婚吗？

410
00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.600
And I expected him to say, you know, I'm really honored you thought of me.
我以为他会说，你知道的，我很荣幸你能想到我。

411
00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:26.060
I don't really have the time.
我真的没时间。

412
00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:26.880
You know, congratulations.
你知道的，祝贺你们。

413
00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.000
I hope you two have a great life.
希望你们俩过上美好的生活。

414
00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:33.540
But he got very, very excited about it.
但他对此感到非常非常兴奋。

415
00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.100
Like, he might be as excited about it as we are.
感觉他可能和我们一样兴奋。

416
00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.700
And went and got himself ordained.
然后去把自己按规定受了神职。

417
00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:41.620
And, yeah, he can't wait for the day just like us.
而且，是的，他跟我们一样迫不及待地期待那一天的到来。

418
00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:42.200
Yeah.
对。

419
00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:43.940
It's so amazing.
太神奇了。

420
00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.920
I'm so excited for you all.
我为你们所有人都感到兴奋。

421
00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.920
Several people have come up to me and they're like,
好几个人过来找我，他们说，

422
00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:52.020
you should come talk to him because they're getting married here at the convention.
你应该来跟他聊聊，因为他们要在漫展这里结婚。

423
00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:54.720
Like, it is a huge buzz this weekend.
就像，这成了这个周末的一个巨大热点。

424
00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.460
We're going to press tons of photos.
我们要拍大量的照片。

425
00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.480
Are you planning to cosplay as you get married?
你们打算cosplay结婚吗？

426
00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.320
Or will you be yourself?
还是做回你们自己？

427
00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:02.300
Oh, no.
噢，不。

428
00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:04.060
We're going to be Dwight and Angela.
我们要扮演德怀特和安吉拉。

429
00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:04.480
Yeah.
对。

430
00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:09.180
Tonight, I'm using foam board and duct tape to make a makeshift coffin.
今晚，我用泡沫板和强力胶带做一个临时的棺材。

431
00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.920
And that's what we're going to be standing in when we're married.
这就是我们结婚时要站立在里面的东西。

432
00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.480
Because that's the best you can do on a hard convention floor, you know.
因为在坚硬的漫展地板上，这已经是你能做到的极限了，你知道的。

433
00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:16.420
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

434
00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:17.360
I know, right?
就是说啊，对吧？

435
00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:18.260
Wow.
哇。

436
00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:18.940
It's amazing.
太棒了。

437
00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:21.760
And how great that Andy Buckley was just like, I got this.
安迪·巴克利直接说“包在我身上”，这太棒了。

438
00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:22.500
I'm here for you.
我为你而来。

439
00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:25.100
I was able to arrive early that day.
我那天能够早点到达。

440
00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.680
And they were doing all their wedding photos right after they got married.
他们刚结完婚就在拍所有的结婚照。

441
00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.060
And I took pictures with them.
我和他们一起拍了照片。

442
00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.000
Oh, amazing.
哦，太棒了。

443
00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:34.760
And they had two best men who were dressed as Moe's and Michael Scott.
他们有两个伴郎，分别打扮成莫斯和迈克尔·斯科特。

444
00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:35.500
Wow.
哇。

445
00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.320
That is so cool.
这太酷了。

446
00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.600
You got pictures, too?
你也有拍照吗？

447
00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:39.800
Can you put them in stories?
你能把它们发到快拍里吗？

448
00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:41.160
Yeah, I absolutely will.
好的，我一定会发的。

449
00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.800
But a lot of people are dressed up as different office characters.
不过很多人都打扮成《办公室》里不同的角色。

450
00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:47.940
One of the gals that helped work my booth, Betty Jean, she's the sweeteSt.
帮我照看展位的其中一个姑娘贝蒂·简，她人最好了。

451
00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:51.880
She told me that she first attended a convention doing cosplay of Pam.
她告诉我她第一次去漫展时cos的是帕姆。

452
00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:54.920
Sam, you've done cosplay at conventions.
萨姆，你也曾在漫展上cos过。

453
00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:59.720
And while I'm slightly afraid to ask this question, would you like to share some of the characters
虽然我有点不敢问这个问题，但你愿意分享一些你

454
00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.000
you've dressed up as?
扮演过的角色吗？

455
00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:03.180
I know Big Titty Gandalf is one.
我知道“巨乳甘道夫”是其中之一。

456
00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.840
Is that the official name of that one?
那是那个角色的官方名字吗？

457
00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.860
Yes, Big Titty Gandalf is the name of the character.
是的，“巨乳甘道夫”就是那个角色的名字。

458
00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:13.240
My personal favorites are, I went as Ash from Evil Dead when I met Bruce Campbell.
我个人最喜欢的是，我去见布鲁斯·坎贝尔时cos了《鬼玩人》里的艾什。

459
00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:20.580
I just met Tim Curry last weekend, dressed as Georgie from It with the missing one arm
我上周末刚见过蒂姆·克里，当时我cos了《小丑回魂》里的乔治，少了一条胳膊

460
00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:22.460
and the bloodied raincoat.
还穿着沾血的雨衣。

461
00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:25.060
Other than that, I think those are my favorite.
除此之外，我想这些就是我最喜欢的了。

462
00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.760
Do you have any plans to go to a convention?
你有什么去漫展的计划吗？

463
00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:28.900
Do you have another one coming up?
你最近还有要去漫展吗？

464
00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:29.380
I do.
有的。

465
00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:34.520
I'm meeting Robert Englund, who was Freddy Krueger, in January and the Fonz in the same
我一月份要见罗伯特·英格兰德，也就是弗莱迪·克鲁格的扮演者，同一天

466
00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:34.720
day.
还要见丰兹。

467
00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:36.580
So I'm going to try and go as the Fonz.
所以我打算尝试cos成丰兹去。

468
00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:37.960
You're going to meet Henry Winkler?
你要去见亨利·温克勒？

469
00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:38.240
Yeah.
