00:37:08.620 --> 00:37:10.640
And it's like, no, we got the New York office.
但实际情况是，不，我们还有纽约办公室。

939
00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:12.780
We had Oscar's apartment.
我们有奥斯卡的公寓。

940
00:37:12.960 --> 00:37:13.840
We had Gabe's apartment.
我们有盖布的公寓。

941
00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:15.040
We had everything, you know?
我们什么都有，你知道吗？

942
00:37:15.100 --> 00:37:16.440
The warehouse set was huge.
仓库的布景非常巨大。

943
00:37:16.540 --> 00:37:20.680
And then we had all the other district offices, Nashua and all these other ones.
然后我们还有所有其他的地区分公司，纳什亚以及所有这些地方。

944
00:37:21.180 --> 00:37:25.700
So, I mean, you know, we went into empty office buildings, recreated those, and made all
所以，我的意思是，你知道的，我们走进空旷的办公大楼，重新搭建它们，制作各种

945
00:37:25.700 --> 00:37:27.220
kinds of graphics and everything, you know?
各样的图表和一切，你知道吗？

946
00:37:27.300 --> 00:37:28.340
The Dunder Mifflin graphics.
邓德米弗林的图表。

947
00:37:28.680 --> 00:37:30.660
And it was just such a fun thing to do.
这真的是一件非常有趣的事情。

948
00:37:31.100 --> 00:37:34.140
Do you have, like, a favorite set that you created?
你有没有最喜欢的自己搭建的布景？

949
00:37:35.440 --> 00:37:37.040
Well, this was behind Jenna's desk.
嗯，这个就在珍娜的桌子后面。

950
00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:37.520
Hi, Jenna.
嗨，珍娜。

951
00:37:38.620 --> 00:37:39.380
I'll show you.
我来给你看。

952
00:37:39.780 --> 00:37:40.820
It was this right here.
就是这个，在这里。

953
00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:44.760
This is a certificate of participation with James' name on it.
这是一个写着詹姆斯名字的参与证书。

954
00:37:44.900 --> 00:37:45.260
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

955
00:37:45.260 --> 00:37:45.980
It's right behind.
就在后面。

956
00:37:48.360 --> 00:37:51.280
If you hear this screaming, it's a pretzel eating conteSt.
如果你听到这个尖叫声，那是吃软 pretzel 比赛。

957
00:37:52.060 --> 00:37:53.820
Leslie David Baker just got on stage.
莱斯利·大卫·贝克刚刚上台了。

958
00:37:54.240 --> 00:37:54.580
It's great.
太棒了。

959
00:37:54.980 --> 00:38:00.580
Do you have an office episode that you're like, this one was a pain in my butt to work on?
你有没有觉得哪一集《办公室》让你拍起来觉得特别头疼？

960
00:38:01.560 --> 00:38:05.260
I think the New York corporate office, when we first did it, it was kind of tricky.
我觉得纽约总公司那一集，我们刚开始拍的时候有点棘手。

961
00:38:05.480 --> 00:38:08.220
But it was mostly hallway and a couple in a lobby.
但大部分都是走廊和大堂里的几个镜头。

962
00:38:08.380 --> 00:38:09.560
It wasn't so bad.
其实也还好。

963
00:38:09.880 --> 00:38:13.480
We put a lot of detail into Gabe's apartment, and that was a really nice set.
我们在盖布的公寓里投入了很多细节，那是一个非常棒的布景。

964
00:38:14.020 --> 00:38:14.900
Yeah, that was a good one.
对，那一集很不错。

965
00:38:15.040 --> 00:38:17.320
That's when Dwight picked up the baby and it stopped crying.
就是在那一集里，德怀特抱起婴儿，婴儿就不哭了。

966
00:38:17.460 --> 00:38:19.240
In real life, the baby stopped crying.
现实生活中，那个婴儿真的不哭了。

967
00:38:19.500 --> 00:38:21.080
It was a good one take, man.
一条过，真是太棒了。

968
00:38:21.460 --> 00:38:24.180
And then that was a real nice set.
而且那个布景真的很不错。

969
00:38:24.700 --> 00:38:27.360
And Oscars, we put a lot of thought in the Oscars apartment.
还有奥斯卡的公寓，我们在奥斯卡的公寓上花了很多心思。

970
00:38:27.780 --> 00:38:31.560
We actually had a bathroom in there that we did a nice job, and they never shot in the bathroom.
我们实际上在里面做了一个很不错的浴室，但他们从来没有在浴室里拍过镜头。

971
00:38:31.680 --> 00:38:32.020
Oh, no!
哦，不会吧！

972
00:38:32.140 --> 00:38:32.280
Yeah.
是啊。

973
00:38:33.860 --> 00:38:36.300
But they were really good people to us.
但他们对我们真的很好。

974
00:38:36.460 --> 00:38:37.940
I mean, everybody was cool to work with.
我的意思是，每个人合作起来都很棒。

975
00:38:38.140 --> 00:38:38.260
Yeah.
对。

976
00:38:38.660 --> 00:38:40.120
All the actors were really nice.
所有的演员都非常好。

977
00:38:40.280 --> 00:38:40.740
I mean, everybody.
我是说，每个人都是。

978
00:38:40.740 --> 00:38:41.260
That's great.
太好了。

979
00:38:42.440 --> 00:38:43.240
Last question.
最后一个问题。

980
00:38:43.900 --> 00:38:46.480
So, you go in and you create the set.
那么，你们进去搭建布景。

981
00:38:46.660 --> 00:38:50.100
When they're actually shooting, do you stay on set during the shoot?
当他们真正开拍时，你们会留在片场吗？

982
00:38:50.320 --> 00:38:51.820
Yeah, he's called an on-set dresser.
对，有个人叫现场道具师。

983
00:38:51.900 --> 00:38:52.800
He stays with the camera.
他一直跟着摄像机。

984
00:38:52.800 --> 00:38:56.360
But we come in in the morning, get there early, and the guys clean all the sets.
但我们早上会很早就到，大家会把所有的布景清理干净。

985
00:38:56.480 --> 00:38:58.360
They vacuum and dust and clean up everything.
他们会吸尘、除尘，把所有东西都收拾好。

986
00:38:58.560 --> 00:39:05.260
But, you know, we'll leave all Stanley's crossword puzzles on his desk and make sure Creed has his solitaire game up.
不过，你知道的，我们会把斯坦利所有的填字游戏都留在他的桌上，还要确保克里德的纸牌游戏开着。

987
00:39:05.440 --> 00:39:08.900
And I have a guy that comes in and cleans the computers every week, an IT guy.
我每周都会请一个人来清理电脑，是个 IT 人员。

988
00:39:09.060 --> 00:39:09.340
Yeah.
对。

989
00:39:09.540 --> 00:39:12.140
And we had live plants in there, so it was nothing fake.
我们在那里放的都是活植物，没有一个是假的。

990
00:39:12.320 --> 00:39:19.280
So, I got the order for the Boise paper, and they gave us script paper, gave us pallets of paper every month.
所以，我接到了博伊西纸业的订单，他们给我们剧本纸，每个月给我们提供一托盘一托盘的纸。

991
00:39:19.280 --> 00:39:22.360
So, probably saved them millions of dollars on paper alone.
所以，光是在纸张上可能就为他们省下了数百万美元。

992
00:39:22.760 --> 00:39:26.080
And then we would take the empty boxes and put them in the warehouse set on pallets.
然后我们会把空箱子放在仓库布景的托盘上。

993
00:39:26.220 --> 00:39:26.520
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

994
00:39:26.540 --> 00:39:28.820
So, all those boxes in the warehouse set were empty.
所以，仓库布景里的所有箱子其实都是空的。

995
00:39:29.180 --> 00:39:29.460
Whoa.
哇。

996
00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:29.940
Yeah.
是的。

997
00:39:30.360 --> 00:39:33.800
When they had to go through some and load up, we put little sandbags in them.
当他们必须搬运一些箱子装车时，我们在里面放了小沙袋。

998
00:39:34.020 --> 00:39:34.220
Oh.
哦。

999
00:39:34.260 --> 00:39:34.780
Full of sand.
里面装满了沙子。

1000
00:39:35.020 --> 00:39:36.880
So, when they dropped it, it sounded like it was heavy.
所以当他们把箱子放下时，听起来就像是很重一样。

1001
00:39:37.440 --> 00:39:37.820
Okay.
好吧。

1002
00:39:38.420 --> 00:39:42.600
And then all the props we got, like, remember the Froggy sticker next to Dwight's desk?
还有我们收集的所有道具，比如，还记得德怀特办公桌旁边的青蛙贴纸吗？

1003
00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:43.600
I put that on there.
那是我贴上去的。

1004
00:39:43.860 --> 00:39:44.120
Oh.
哦。

1005
00:39:44.120 --> 00:39:44.320
Yeah.
对。

1006
00:39:44.320 --> 00:39:46.300
So, we got in touch.
所以，我们联系上了。

1007
00:39:46.460 --> 00:39:53.360
We were trying to figure out how to use things from Scranton, so I suggested we call Marry Potis is her name.
我们当时在想怎么利用斯克兰顿的东西，于是我建议给一个叫玛丽·波蒂斯的人打电话。

1008
00:39:53.520 --> 00:39:55.260
She's the Chamber of Commerce president.
她是商会会长。

1009
00:39:55.480 --> 00:39:58.840
And we're like, can we get some local Scranton goods from your local businesses?
我们就问，能不能从你们当地企业那里弄到一些斯克兰顿的特色商品？

1010
00:39:59.120 --> 00:40:00.140
But they got to sign off.
但他们得签字批准。

1011
00:40:00.240 --> 00:40:01.820
And we thought we'd get, like, three or four boxes.
而且我们本以为能拿到三四箱左右。

1012
00:40:01.820 --> 00:40:03.420
So, we got ten pallets of stuff.
结果，我们弄到了十托盘的东西。

1013
00:40:03.560 --> 00:40:03.880
Oh, my gosh.
我的天哪。

1014
00:40:04.080 --> 00:40:04.260
Yeah.
对啊。

1015
00:40:04.400 --> 00:40:04.580
Whoa.
哇。

1016
00:40:04.840 --> 00:40:05.620
Tons of stuff.
超级多的东西。

1017
00:40:05.840 --> 00:40:06.540
That's amazing.
太厉害了。

1018
00:40:06.640 --> 00:40:06.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1019
00:40:07.120 --> 00:40:08.740
So, we used a lot of it.
所以，我们用了很多。

1020
00:40:09.160 --> 00:40:11.340
The refrigerator had all kinds of menus on it.
冰箱上贴满了各种菜单。

1021
00:40:11.820 --> 00:40:13.440
Alfredo's Pizza is a real pizzeria.
阿尔弗雷德披萨店是一家真正的比萨店。

1022
00:40:13.440 --> 00:40:13.680
Yeah.
对。

1023
00:40:14.080 --> 00:40:14.480
Yeah.
没错。

1024
00:40:14.680 --> 00:40:17.740
So, I ended up meeting a lot of people that I was friends with in Scranton.
所以，我最后见到了很多我在斯克兰顿的好朋友。

1025
00:40:17.820 --> 00:40:20.560
So, I'm going to go to the 5K next year.
因此，我打算明年去参加五公里长跑。

1026
00:40:20.860 --> 00:40:21.280
Yeah.
好啊。

1027
00:40:21.500 --> 00:40:22.280
I want to go.
我也想去。

1028
00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:23.400
I wish Jenna was here.
我真希望珍娜也在。

1029
00:40:23.480 --> 00:40:24.380
I hope Jenna's doing okay.
希望珍娜一切都好。

1030
00:40:24.540 --> 00:40:24.980
Hi, Jenna.
嗨，珍娜。

1031
00:40:25.280 --> 00:40:25.500
Yeah.
对。

1032
00:40:25.600 --> 00:40:26.240
She's doing okay.
她挺好的。

1033
00:40:26.240 --> 00:40:29.460
She's working on a play in Chicago now.
她现在在芝加哥排练一部话剧。

1034
00:40:29.580 --> 00:40:29.860
Oh, gotcha.
哦，明白了。

1035
00:40:29.920 --> 00:40:30.340
That's great.
太棒了。

1036
00:40:31.140 --> 00:40:35.960
I love that detail that he shared about the pallets in the warehouse.
我好喜欢他分享的关于仓库里那些托盘的细节。

1037
00:40:35.960 --> 00:40:42.720
That we got all that free paper that we use to print our scripts every week, and then they
我们拿到了所有那些免费纸张，用来每周打印我们的剧本，然后他们

1038
00:40:42.720 --> 00:40:43.720
just filled them with sandbags.
只是在里面装满了沙袋。

1039
00:40:43.820 --> 00:40:44.580
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

1040
00:40:44.780 --> 00:40:46.240
All those boxes were empty.
原来那些箱子都是空的。

1041
00:40:46.420 --> 00:40:46.620
Yeah.
对。

1042
00:40:46.620 --> 00:40:47.020
That's so cool.
太酷了。

1043
00:40:47.020 --> 00:40:51.520
I just assumed all those were actually filled with paper, I guess.
我还以为那些箱子里真的都装满了纸呢。

1044
00:40:51.860 --> 00:40:51.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1045
00:40:52.160 --> 00:40:53.080
Because they were heavy.
因为它们挺重的。

1046
00:40:53.440 --> 00:40:56.600
Well, I remember Oscar's apartment with such detail.
说到奥斯卡的那套公寓，细节真的太丰富了。

1047
00:40:56.600 --> 00:41:03.640
I took a bunch of pictures of it because I was doing a home renovation, and I was like,
我拍了好多照片，因为我当时在装修房子，然后我就……

1048
00:41:03.640 --> 00:41:05.620
I realized they didn't do a single scene in the bathroom.
我发现他们甚至没有在浴室里拍过一场戏。

1049
00:41:06.160 --> 00:41:10.880
You know, they built a whole bathroom set for Ashland Avenue because our characters walk
你知道的，他们为阿什兰大道搭建了一整套浴室布景，因为我们的角色偶尔会

1050
00:41:10.880 --> 00:41:16.240
in there from time to time, but only like this tiny sliver of the audience could see it.
走进去，但其实只有极小一部分观众能看到它。

1051
00:41:16.340 --> 00:41:22.840
It was literally like 12 seats could see into the bathroom, but they built a whole bathroom.
真的就像有12个座位能直接看到洗手间，但他们还是建了一个完整的洗手间。

1052
00:41:23.340 --> 00:41:28.380
I was really appreciative of it because otherwise I would have been like walking backstage and
我真的很感激，因为不然的话我可能得走到后台去，

1053
00:41:28.380 --> 00:41:31.620
just kind of pretending I was in a bathroom, but I could stand in a real bathroom.
然后假装自己在上厕所，但我可以站在一个真正的洗手间里。

1054
00:41:31.680 --> 00:41:32.400
That's cool.
那太酷了。

1055
00:41:32.400 --> 00:41:34.100
I did not see the bathroom set.
我没看到那个洗手间布景。

1056
00:41:34.640 --> 00:41:35.180
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1057
00:41:35.300 --> 00:41:36.340
Literally 12 people.
真的只有12个人。

1058
00:41:36.560 --> 00:41:40.700
Like our director, Susan Booth, she'd always be like, okay, Jenna, exit to the bathroom.
就像我们的导演苏珊·布思，她总是会说，好吧，珍娜，退场去洗手间。

1059
00:41:40.840 --> 00:41:42.900
12 people will get to see what you're doing in there.
会有12个人看到你在里面做什么。

1060
00:41:43.020 --> 00:41:45.340
So don't forget, you got to keep acting while you're in there.
所以别忘了，你在里面的时候还得继续演。

1061
00:41:45.600 --> 00:41:45.960
Wow.
哇。

1062
00:41:45.960 --> 00:41:46.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1063
00:41:46.440 --> 00:41:47.220
That's so cool.
太酷了。

1064
00:41:47.580 --> 00:41:50.480
Oh, and Jim gave me something to give to you too.
哦，吉姆还让我带了样东西给你。

1065
00:41:50.800 --> 00:41:51.320
He did?
是吗？

1066
00:41:51.560 --> 00:41:51.800
What?
什么？

1067
00:41:52.020 --> 00:41:52.070
Yeah.
对。

1068
00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:55.160
So he gave me the daily call sheet for the pilot.
他把试播集的每日通告单给我了。

1069
00:41:56.160 --> 00:41:56.880
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

1070
00:41:57.300 --> 00:41:57.660
Wow.
哇。

1071
00:41:58.220 --> 00:42:01.000
And it's like the, oh my goodness.
而且这个，哦天哪。

1072
00:42:01.080 --> 00:42:01.740
You know what?
你知道吗？

1073
00:42:01.740 --> 00:42:04.100
I have this as a digital thing.
我有这个的电子版。

1074
00:42:04.560 --> 00:42:05.040
All right.
好的。

1075
00:42:05.100 --> 00:42:05.200
Yeah.
对。

1076
00:42:05.280 --> 00:42:11.640
So this is the call sheet for, it says day 2.5 of 5.5.
所以这是通告单，上面写着第2.5天，总共5.5天。

1077
00:42:12.080 --> 00:42:13.560
So day two of the pilot.
也就是试播集的第二天。

1078
00:42:13.760 --> 00:42:15.640
Here's what it says under set dressing.
场景布置那一栏是这样写的。

1079
00:42:15.880 --> 00:42:22.500
It says that they're going to need a coat rack, a Homer Simpson doll, an office plant, and a
上面说他们需要一个衣帽架、一个荷马·辛普森玩偶、一盆办公室绿植，以及

1080
00:42:22.500 --> 00:42:24.060
Billy Bass fish on the wall.
墙上的一条比利大口黑鲈鱼。

1081
00:42:24.800 --> 00:42:27.880
I didn't realize the Billy Bass fish went that far back.
我没想到比利大口黑鲈鱼从那么早就有了。

1082
00:42:27.880 --> 00:42:29.120
It does, I guess.
看来是的。

1083
00:42:29.780 --> 00:42:30.120
All right.
好吧。

1084
00:42:30.180 --> 00:42:34.520
Well, listen, since we're giving gifts, I have stuff that people gave me at the stage
听着，既然大家都在送礼物，我有大家在剧院门口送给你们的

1085
00:42:34.520 --> 00:42:35.820
door for all of you.
东西。

1086
00:42:36.320 --> 00:42:38.000
Angela, I'm going to start with you.
安吉拉，我从你开始。

1087
00:42:38.780 --> 00:42:43.500
Jackie gifted us the cutest Chicago-inspired sweatshirts.
杰基送了我们超可爱的芝加哥风情卫衣。

1088
00:42:43.620 --> 00:42:45.660
She makes these on her Etsy shop.
她在自己的Etsy店铺里制作这些。

1089
00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:47.800
It's called Jacqueline Louise, please.
店名叫“杰奎琳·路易丝，拜托”。

1090
00:42:48.480 --> 00:42:51.980
She made you a Chicago deep dish pizza sweatshirt.
她为你做了一件芝加哥深盘披萨卫衣。

1091
00:42:51.980 --> 00:42:54.980
Oh, deep dish pizza sounds really good right now.
哦，现在听起来深盘披萨真的很诱人。

1092
00:42:55.660 --> 00:42:57.960
She made me a Chicago hot dog.
她给我做了一个芝加哥热狗。

1093
00:42:58.240 --> 00:43:02.660
I loved the Chicago hot dogs when I was there, so I'm very excited that she gave me the hot
我呆在芝加哥时特别喜欢那里的热狗，所以她送我热狗款我真的超级兴奋。

1094
00:43:02.660 --> 00:43:03.140
dog one.
